        // P020 empty-sleep probe below, so it deleted the only instrument that ever told these calls apart: an off-thread
        // create-then-sleep (0x7F381F / 0x7F7CC3 / the addUnloadedSquad site - empty by construction, nothing is lost)
        // and Faction::_switchToUnloadedPlatoon 0x6B94CB reached from GameWorld::destroy on a streaming worker (which can
        // carry MEMBERS, and whose delete-at-sleep is then never written) both produce one anonymous +1. The rva says which.
        // First only per caller, eight slots, claimed with an interlock because several workers can be here at once. The
        // pod read is the SEH-guarded one and touches no shared container, so it is safe here - it is the map work below
        // that was not, and activeChars is the whole difference between "a harmless empty" and "a group lost its note".
