// changed the cause string on it, from `teardown` to `stale-lease`. This is review-p6j HIGH-1, and the fix is at
// the loss rather than at the gate: WHILE THE NOTEBOOK PROCESS IS LINKED THE AREA MAP IS KEPT THROUGH A TEARDOWN.
// Why that is safe and better, stated rather than assumed. The relay republishes the whole map every second and
// ApplyRelayAreaMap replaces all four grids and both clocks wholesale.
// P6x (review-p6q MEDIUM-3) - THE BOUND IS 5 s SINCE THE LAST AREAMAP, NOT ONE SECOND, and the difference matters
// in both directions. One second is the relay's PUBLICATION interval; 5 s is the staleness cap every reader of
// these clocks applies (HostHoldsSectorTS, OtherLoadedTS, MineHeldTS, RelayMapFresh and AreaViewTS all answer -1
// past it). So the kept map CANNOT FREEZE - it expires by itself 5 s after the last AREAMAP whether or not a
// teardown happened - and equally this repair covers a world load only for as long as 5 s. A load blocks the main
// thread and PumpLink is on the main-thread tick, so no AREAMAP lands during one; if the new world's towns are
// generated more than 5 s after the last map that arrived before the teardown, held is -1 again and a declared
